---
description: How to write and change ArtScript (.art) code in this project
globs: **/*.art
alwaysApply: false
---

This project is written in ArtScript. Before writing `.art` code, read `ARTSCRIPT-CORE.md` (~1,600 tokens, a whole app as the example); `ARTSCRIPT.md` is the full reference when you need the backend, accounts or relations in detail; to only change existing code, `ARTSCRIPT-EDIT.md` (~800 tokens) is enough.

- After every change run `npx art check --ai` and fix what it reports (each error has `expected` and `fixes`).
- Read `npx art context <Component>` instead of whole files; prefer a small `art patch` to rewriting files.
- Write `test "..." { }` blocks for the main flows and run `npx art test`.
- Expressions are JavaScript; only the structure (`page`, `component`, `model`, `api`, `state`, `data`, `fn`, the view) is ArtScript's own.
- Heavy imperative code (a physics loop, a parser, canvas drawing) goes in a `.ts` file next to the `.art` files, imported with `use "./sim.ts" { step, draw }`: plain TypeScript, no restrictions. ArtScript is for the page, the state, the api, forms, lists and tests. Measured: with this rule an agent writes the ArtScript page as fluently as a React one.
